From ce9fe7fd2062d5b124fd7ad8afee91bb795ff11c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:06:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] fix(gateway): answer every gateway error with the JSON
 envelope

The rate limiter's 429, the 502 when the reverse proxy or the stream
proxy gets no response from the control plane or an instance, and
net/http's default 404 for paths no route matches were plain text,
without a code, a correlation id or a trace id, unlike the gateway's
other errors. Clients had to special-case them, and the response
could not be matched to the logs by its body.

They now use the shared envelope with stable codes: RATE_LIMITED
(Retry-After is unchanged), UPSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE, INVALID_UPSTREAM
when the request to an instance cannot be built, and NOT_FOUND for
unknown paths. Under /api/v1/ the 404 still goes through the whole
chain; elsewhere it gets the correlation id, the trace id and an
access log line but, as before, no authentication or rate limit.
/metrics answers methods other than GET and HEAD with
METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED. Status codes and existing codes are unchanged,
and responses from the control plane or instances pass through
untouched.
